STEP 0 - param ContextId:
New namespace per owner kind in app_data.c (DATA_NS_CLAP_PARAM/DATA_NS_
LV2_PARAM/DATA_NS_SYNTH_PARAM/DATA_NS_SAMPLE_PARAM), mirroring the
existing per-kind instance namespaces. A param's .id() is a flat one-
liner, MAKE_ID(that_ns, param_get_uid(container, val_id, 0)) - no
folding/hash-chaining needed, since a param's uid is already globally
unique for its whole kind (this session's next_param_uid fix). Safe at
any future nesting depth for the same reason.

STEP 1 - params exist structurally, nothing displays them:
Real child_count/child_at for clap_plugin_ops (first), skipping
tombstoned (NULL) slots, params' .id() from STEP 0, hidden params
included too. capabilities = 0 otherwise - no NAME/VALUE/ACTIONS yet.
Verify via build+valgrind/pty harness before the live CLI; confirm
