STEP 2 - structural add/remove events:
Per-instance params_dirty bool (distinct from the container-level
plugins_dirty), set right after params_container_resync, checked in
clap_read_rt_to_ui_messages. app_data_update turns it into DATA_EVENT_
CHILDREN_CHANGED, mirroring the existing plugins_dirty handling exactly.
Fulfills clap_plugins.c's own "TODO (STAGE 3): flag this instance's
params_dirty here" at the CLAP_PARAM_RESCAN_ALL branch. The CX diff
itself (CX_ADDED/CX_REMOVED) is already fully generic - no new code
there. LV2/sampler/synth's params don't change shape after creation, so
their flag can stay unconditionally false for now, same precedent as
synth's own instance-level dirty flag.

STEP 3 - UI shows names, values, and range:
- DATA_CAP_NAME/name() - param_get_name.
- DATA_CAP_VALUE/value_as_string() - param_get_value_as_string, with a
  fallback added: format the raw value as a plain number when the owner
  registered no val_to_string (sampler and LV2 do params_init_param_
  container(NULL) today - no callback at all). Decimal count derived
  from the param's own increment: smallest d where inc*10^d is (within
  an epsilon) a whole number, capped at 6 - inc=1 -> 0 decimals, inc=
  0.001 -> 3. Fulfills plugins.c's own "TODO val_to_string callback...
  can be added here whenever something actually calls param_get_value_
  as_string" - decided: LV2 uses the raw-numeric fallback only, no
  custom formatter.
- value_range() (min, max, inc) - same DATA_CAP_VALUE capability,
  bundled with value_as_string() as one query.

STEP 4 - UI can change values:
- DATA_ARG_NUMBER added to DataArgKind (data_actions.h currently has
  only STRING/PATH/CHOICE/MULTI_CHOICE) - needed before SET_VALUE/
  ADJUST_VALUE can declare their arg via action_args.
- DATA_ACTION_SET_VALUE (absolute) + DATA_ACTION_ADJUST_VALUE (signed
  step count, not a raw value - action_do maps sign to Operation_
  Increase/Decrease) - one-line param_set_value calls in action_do.
- DATA_ACTION_SET_CHOICE for CLAP_PARAM_IS_ENUM params - reuse list_at/
  DataChoice/helper_choice_list_step as-is, list_at walks min..max
  calling param_get_value_as_string per step for the label.
- DATA_CAP_HIDDEN/is_hidden() as a query ONLY - no DATA_ACTION_TOGGLE_
  HIDDEN. is_hidden reflects the plugin's own classification, not a user
  preference - a future "user hides/shows something in their own view"
  concept, if built, should be its own separate mechanism, not reuse
  this.
- IS_READONLY gating on SET_VALUE/ADJUST_VALUE/SET_CHOICE's DataAction.
  enabled, generalized per owner: CLAP's CLAP_PARAM_IS_READONLY flag,
  LV2's cur_ctrl->is_writable == 0 (fulfills plugins.c's own "TODO now
  if the param is not writable... it should have a property for this
  parameter to not send it to ui_to_rt ring buffer" - achieved via
  action-gating rather than literally suppressing the ring-buffer send).

- Flags system (replaces the single is_hidden bool, fulfills params.c's
  own pre-existing "TODO instead of is hidden implement flag system"):
  new enum paramFlags in params.h, own independent bit numbering (not
  CLAP's - params.h stays owner-agnostic, same reasoning as owner_id),
  doc-commented per bit, only what's implemented now:
    PARAM_FLAG_HIDDEN   = 1 << 0
    PARAM_FLAG_READONLY = 1 << 1
  PRM_PARAM_UI.is_hidden (uint16_t) -> PRM_PARAM_UI.flags (uint32_t,
  matching clap_param_info_flags' width). param_add_param gains a
  uint32_t flags parameter (every call site updated: clap_plugins.c,
  plugins.c, sampler.c, synth.c, params_container_resync's own pass-2
  call - 0 where a module has no flag source yet). PARAM_RESYNC_ITEM
  gains a matching flags field. Operation_ToggleHidden renamed/
  repurposed to Operation_SetFlags (sets the WHOLE flags value to
  set_to, not a single-bit toggle - reconciliation below hands the
  plugin's current full flag state wholesale, not a delta). param_is_
  hidden stays (now backed by flags & PARAM_FLAG_HIDDEN); new param_is_
  readonly added the same way.

  Fulfills clap_plugins.c's two flags-related TODOs. Both need their own
  reconciliation, since RESCAN_INFO and RESCAN_ALL can fire independently
  of each other:
  - clap_plug_discover_params's empty CLAP_PARAM_IS_HIDDEN block:
    translate CLAP_PARAM_IS_HIDDEN/CLAP_PARAM_IS_READONLY into PARAM_
    RESYNC_ITEM.flags for every discovered param. New adds get correct
    initial flags straight from param_add_param - no follow-up needed.
    Survivors are untouched by resync itself (same tombstone-preserving
    guarantee as name/value) so still need reconciling: after params_
    container_resync returns (clap_plug_params_create and RESCAN_ALL),
    walk the discovered list again, and only for entries param_find_uid
    finds already alive, apply Operation_SetFlags with a MASKED merge -
    (current_flags & ~KNOWN_MASK) | (discovered_flags & KNOWN_MASK), not
    a blind overwrite, so a future non-CLAP-sourced flag bit is never
    silently clobbered - only if it differs from current.
  - RESCAN_INFO's own "get if any parameter is hidden or not" TODO: not
    made redundant by the above, since RESCAN_INFO can fire alone without
    RESCAN_ALL - needs the same masked Operation_SetFlags reconciliation
    in its own branch, alongside its existing name check.
  - LV2 needs neither reconciliation pass at all: confirmed LV2 has no
    plugin-to-host "something changed" mechanism in this app at all
    (param_get_if_changed_rt only propagates UI-driven changes OUT to the
    plugin; the one path that could carry a change back - parsing an
    incoming patch:Set atom - is unparsed, plugins.c's own TODO, already
    self-deprioritized). LV2's flags are set once, correctly, at param_
    add_param time and never need touching again.

STEP 5 - UI reacts to individual param changes:
PRM_PARAM_UI gets a ui_changed flag mirroring PRM_PARAM_RT.val_changed,
set by param_msgs_process on a ui-side apply; param_get_if_changed_ui
checks-and-clears it, mirroring param_get_if_changed_rt. params.c and
the owner modules stay ContextId-ignorant - no signature changes to any
*_read_rt_to_ui_messages function. app_data_update polls the flag per
param right after its existing drain calls, same spot/shape as the
plugins_dirty checks, and is the only place that mints the ContextId and
calls app_data_push_event - content-free DATA_EVENT_CHANGED, no value/
name distinction. The current CLI won't consume this (confirmed - full
redraw every cycle, doesn't read CX_CHANGED at all) - pure future-
proofing for a selective-redraw UI.

STEP 6 - categories:
PRM_PARAM_UI gets a category/module string field (CLAP: clap_param_
info_t.module) + accessor. Params stay FLAT CX children - category is
presentational metadata only, not a real tree level. child_at returns
params sorted by category so a UI can print a header over contiguous
runs. CLI-side grouping/header display not yet designed - its own small
pass once this lands.

